---
import "../styles/global.css";
---

<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<meta charset="utf-8" />
		<link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
		<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
		<title>Hauke Schnau — Software Developer</title>
		<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
		<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
		<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Outfit:wght@300;400;500;600&family=Playfair+Display:ital,wght@0,400..900;1,400..900&family=Source+Serif+4:ital,opsz,wght@0,8..60,200..900;1,8..60,200..900&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />
		<style>
			:root {
				--bg: #FAF7F2;
				--text: #1a1a1a;
				--text-secondary: #6b6155;
				--accent: #c1440e;
				--divider: #ddd5c9;
				--pullquote-bg: #f0ebe3;
				--font-display: 'Playfair Display', Georgia, serif;
				--font-body: 'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif;
				--font-label: 'Outfit', system-ui, sans-serif;
			}

			* {
				margin: 0;
				padding: 0;
				box-sizing: border-box;
			}

			html {
				scroll-behavior: smooth;
			}

			body {
				background: var(--bg);
				color: var(--text);
				font-family: var(--font-body);
				font-size: 18px;
				line-height: 1.7;
				-webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
				overflow-x: hidden;
			}

			/* Paper texture noise overlay */
			body::before {
				content: '';
				position: fixed;
				inset: 0;
				z-index: 9999;
				pointer-events: none;
				opacity: 0.025;
				background-image: url("data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg viewBox='0 0 256 256' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%3E%3Cfilter id='noise'%3E%3CfeTurbulence type='fractalNoise' baseFrequency='0.9' numOctaves='4' stitchTiles='stitch'/%3E%3C/filter%3E%3Crect width='100%25' height='100%25' filter='url(%23noise)'/%3E%3C/svg%3E");
				background-repeat: repeat;
				background-size: 256px 256px;
			}

			.fade-in {
				opacity: 0;
				transform: translateY(24px);
				transition: opacity 0.8s cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1), transform 0.8s cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1);
			}
			.fade-in.visible {
				opacity: 1;
				transform: translateY(0);
			}
			.fade-in-left {
				opacity: 0;
				transform: translateX(-30px);
				transition: opacity 0.8s cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1), transform 0.8s cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1);
			}
			.fade-in-left.visible {
				opacity: 1;
				transform: translateX(0);
			}
			.fade-in-right {
				opacity: 0;
				transform: translateX(30px);
				transition: opacity 0.8s cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1), transform 0.8s cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1);
			}
			.fade-in-right.visible {
				opacity: 1;
				transform: translateX(0);
			}

			.delay-1 { transition-delay: 0.1s; }
			.delay-2 { transition-delay: 0.2s; }
			.delay-3 { transition-delay: 0.3s; }
			.delay-4 { transition-delay: 0.4s; }
			.delay-5 { transition-delay: 0.5s; }

			/* Drop cap */
			.drop-cap::first-letter {
				font-family: var(--font-display);
				float: left;
				font-size: 5.2em;
				line-height: 0.8;
				padding-right: 0.08em;
				padding-top: 0.06em;
				color: var(--accent);
				font-weight: 700;
			}

			.editorial-hr {
				border: none;
				height: 1px;
				background: var(--divider);
				margin: 0;
			}

			.editorial-hr-thick {
				border: none;
				height: 2px;
				background: var(--text);
				margin: 0;
			}

			.label {
				font-family: var(--font-label);
				font-size: 11px;
				font-weight: 500;
				letter-spacing: 0.15em;
				text-transform: uppercase;
				color: var(--text-secondary);
			}

			.section-number {
				font-family: var(--font-display);
				font-size: 72px;
				font-weight: 400;
				color: var(--divider);
				line-height: 1;
			}

			.pull-quote {
				font-family: var(--font-display);
				font-style: italic;
				font-size: 28px;
				line-height: 1.4;
				color: var(--text);
				background: var(--pullquote-bg);
				padding: 40px 48px;
				border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
				position: relative;
			}
			.pull-quote::before {
				content: '\201C';
				font-family: var(--font-display);
				font-size: 80px;
				color: var(--accent);
				position: absolute;
				top: 8px;
				left: 16px;
				line-height: 1;
				opacity: 0.3;
			}

			.photo-placeholder {
				background: linear-gradient(145deg, #d6cfc5, #c9c1b4);
				position: relative;
				overflow: hidden;
			}
			.photo-placeholder::after {
				content: '';
				position: absolute;
				inset: 0;
				border: 1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.06);
			}

			.photo-caption {
				font-family: var(--font-label);
				font-size: 12px;
				font-style: italic;
				color: var(--text-secondary);
				margin-top: 8px;
				letter-spacing: 0.02em;
			}

			a {
				color: var(--accent);
				text-decoration: none;
				transition: color 0.2s;
			}
			a:hover {
				color: #a03a0c;
			}

			.magazine-container {
				max-width: 1200px;
				margin: 0 auto;
				padding: 0 24px;
			}

			/* Timeline connector */
			.timeline-item {
				position: relative;
				padding-left: 32px;
			}
			.timeline-item::before {
				content: '';
				position: absolute;
				left: 0;
				top: 10px;
				width: 10px;
				height: 10px;
				border-radius: 50%;
				background: var(--accent);
			}
			.timeline-item::after {
				content: '';
				position: absolute;
				left: 4px;
				top: 24px;
				bottom: -24px;
				width: 1px;
				background: var(--divider);
			}
			.timeline-item:last-child::after {
				display: none;
			}

			/* Tech grid */
			.tech-category h4 {
				font-family: var(--font-label);
				font-size: 11px;
				font-weight: 600;
				letter-spacing: 0.15em;
				text-transform: uppercase;
				color: var(--accent);
				margin-bottom: 8px;
				padding-bottom: 6px;
				border-bottom: 1px solid var(--divider);
			}
			.tech-category p {
				font-family: var(--font-body);
				font-size: 15px;
				line-height: 1.8;
				color: var(--text-secondary);
			}

			/* Blog article card */
			.blog-article {
				padding: 24px 0;
				border-bottom: 1px solid var(--divider);
			}
			.blog-article:last-child {
				border-bottom: none;
			}

			/* Principle blocks */
			.principle-block {
				display: grid;
				grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
				gap: 48px;
				padding: 48px 0;
				border-bottom: 1px solid var(--divider);
				align-items: start;
			}
			.principle-block:last-child {
				border-bottom: none;
			}
			.principle-block.reverse {
				direction: rtl;
			}
			.principle-block.reverse > * {
				direction: ltr;
			}
			.principle-statement {
				font-family: var(--font-display);
				font-style: italic;
				font-size: 26px;
				line-height: 1.35;
				color: var(--text);
				padding-top: 4px;
			}
			.principle-detail {
				font-size: 16px;
				line-height: 1.75;
				color: var(--text-secondary);
			}
			.principle-label {
				font-family: var(--font-label);
				font-size: 10px;
				font-weight: 600;
				letter-spacing: 0.2em;
				text-transform: uppercase;
				color: var(--accent);
				margin-bottom: 12px;
				display: block;
			}
			.read-more {
				font-family: var(--font-label);
				font-size: 12px;
				font-weight: 500;
				letter-spacing: 0.1em;
				text-transform: uppercase;
				color: var(--accent);
				text-decoration: none;
				display: inline-flex;
				align-items: center;
				gap: 6px;
				margin-top: 12px;
				transition: gap 0.2s;
			}
			.read-more:hover {
				gap: 10px;
			}

			@media (max-width: 768px) {
				body { font-size: 16px; }
				.pull-quote {
					font-size: 22px;
					padding: 28px 24px;
				}
				.pull-quote::before {
					font-size: 60px;
					top: 4px;
					left: 8px;
				}
				.drop-cap::first-letter {
					font-size: 4em;
				}
				.section-number {
					font-size: 48px;
				}
				.principle-block,
				.principle-block.reverse {
					grid-template-columns: 1fr;
					gap: 16px;
					direction: ltr;
				}
				.principle-statement {
					font-size: 22px;
				}
			}
		</style>
	</head>
	<body>

		<!-- Back link -->
		<div class="magazine-container" style="padding-top: 20px;">
			<a href="/" class="label" style="color: var(--text-secondary); text-decoration: none; display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px;">
				<span style="font-size: 14px;">←</span> Back to designs
			</a>
		</div>

		<!-- ========================================== -->
		<!-- HEADER -->
		<!-- ========================================== -->
		<header class="magazine-container" style="padding-top: 40px; padding-bottom: 16px;">
			<div class="fade-in" style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 12px;">
				<div style="font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 20px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.02em;">Hauke Schnau</div>
				<div class="label" style="text-align: right;">
					Software Developer · Hamburg
				</div>
			</div>
		</header>
		<div class="magazine-container"><hr class="editorial-hr-thick" /></div>
		<div class="magazine-container" style="padding-top: 6px; padding-bottom: 6px;">
			<div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px;">
				<span class="label" style="font-size: 10px;">TypeScript · React · Go</span>
				<span class="label" style="font-size: 10px;">AI-Native Development</span>
				<span class="label" style="font-size: 10px;">Architecture · Full Stack</span>
			</div>
		</div>
		<div class="magazine-container"><hr class="editorial-hr" /></div>

		<!-- ========================================== -->
		<!-- HERO / COVER -->
		<!-- ========================================== -->
		<section class="magazine-container" style="padding-top: 64px; padding-bottom: 64px;">
			<div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 48px; align-items: end;" class="hero-grid">
				<div class="fade-in">
					<h1 style="font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: clamp(56px, 8vw, 96px); font-weight: 700; line-height: 0.95; letter-spacing: -0.03em; margin-bottom: 24px;">
						Hauke<br/>Schnau
					</h1>
					<div style="font-family: var(--font-label); font-size: 13px; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: 0.2em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--text-secondary); margin-bottom: 32px;">
						Software Developer · Hamburg / Bremen
					</div>
					<hr class="editorial-hr" style="margin-bottom: 24px;" />
					<p style="font-family: var(--font-display); font-style: italic; font-size: 22px; line-height: 1.4; color: var(--text); max-width: 480px;">
						Full-stack TypeScript, end-to-end type safety, and AI-native tooling — building software I can trust at compile time
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="fade-in delay-2">
					<div class="photo-placeholder" style="aspect-ratio: 3/4; width: 100%;"></div>
					<p class="photo-caption">Hauke Schnau, Hamburg, 2026</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<div class="magazine-container"><hr class="editorial-hr" /></div>

		<!-- ========================================== -->
		<!-- THE PROFILE -->
		<!-- ========================================== -->
		<section class="magazine-container" style="padding-top: 72px; padding-bottom: 72px;">
			<div class="fade-in" style="margin-bottom: 48px;">
				<div style="display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 20px; margin-bottom: 12px;">
					<span class="section-number">01</span>
					<div>
						<h2 style="font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 42px; font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.1; letter-spacing: -0.02em;">About Me</h2>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 2fr 1fr; gap: 64px;" class="profile-grid">
				<div>
					<p class="drop-cap fade-in" style="margin-bottom: 24px;">
						I've been writing production code since I was nineteen. It started at homevoice, building property management software with Spring Boot and React. From there I moved to Check24, where I mentioned Zod in my coding challenge and my future team lead's ears perked up — we ended up having a great conversation about type safety and developer tooling.
					</p>

					<p class="fade-in" style="margin-bottom: 24px;">
						At Check24 I worked across React and Symfony, doing code reviews, performance optimization, and shipping features in an established agile team. I left with the company's highest performance rating and an offer to return well above junior level. My current role at Buildlinx takes things further — I lead the frontend, shape architecture decisions, and work across the stack from TypeScript to Go for an IoT building management platform.
					</p>

					<p class="fade-in" style="margin-bottom: 24px;">
						What really drives me is the modern TypeScript ecosystem — Effect TS, tRPC, Zod, and end-to-end type safety. I follow Theo (t3.gg) and the broader web community closely, and I spend a lot of my free time experimenting with new tools and patterns. My goal is always the same: if it compiles, it should work.
					</p>

					<p class="fade-in" style="margin-bottom: 0;">
						My daily workflow is AI-native. OpenAI Codex handles the bulk of my implementation — I give it well-specified tasks and it delivers code I'm comfortable merging after review. Cursor's Tab completion kicks in when I write code by hand. Claude helps me think through design decisions. I've found that AI is most useful when you know exactly what to ask for, so I spend more time defining tasks precisely than writing code directly.
					</p>
				</div>

				<aside class="fade-in-right delay-3" style="padding-top: 20px;">
					<div style="border-left: 2px solid var(--accent); padding-left: 20px; margin-bottom: 32px;">
						<div class="label" style="margin-bottom: 6px;">Location</div>
						<p style="font-size: 15px; color: var(--text);">Hamburg / Bremen</p>
					</div>
					<div style="border-left: 2px solid var(--divider); padding-left: 20px; margin-bottom: 32px;">
						<div class="label" style="margin-bottom: 6px;">Education</div>
						<p style="font-size: 15px; color: var(--text);">B.Sc. Computer Science<br/>Universität Hamburg (1.47)</p>
					</div>
					<div style="border-left: 2px solid var(--divider); padding-left: 20px; margin-bottom: 32px;">
						<div class="label" style="margin-bottom: 6px;">Current Role</div>
						<p style="font-size: 15px; color: var(--text);">Frontend Lead & Architect<br/>Buildlinx GmbH</p>
					</div>
					<div style="border-left: 2px solid var(--divider); padding-left: 20px;">
						<div class="label" style="margin-bottom: 6px;">Professional Experience</div>
						<p style="font-size: 15px; color: var(--text);">3+ years across 4 companies</p>
					</div>
				</aside>
			</div>
		</section>

		<div class="magazine-container"><hr class="editorial-hr" /></div>

		<!-- ========================================== -->
		<!-- TECH STACK -->
		<!-- ========================================== -->
		<section class="magazine-container" style="padding-top: 72px; padding-bottom: 72px;">
			<div class="fade-in" style="display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 20px; margin-bottom: 48px;">
				<span class="section-number">02</span>
				<div>
					<h2 style="font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 42px; font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.1; letter-spacing: -0.02em;">Tech Stack</h2>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 32px 48px;" class="tech-grid">
				<div class="tech-category fade-in delay-1">
					<h4>Languages</h4>
					<p>TypeScript (primary), Go, PHP, Python, Java</p>
				</div>
				<div class="tech-category fade-in delay-2">
					<h4>Frontend</h4>
					<p>React, React Native, Next.js, Expo, Tailwind CSS, shadcn/ui</p>
				</div>
				<div class="tech-category fade-in delay-3">
					<h4>Backend</h4>
					<p>Node.js, Bun, tRPC, Drizzle ORM, Symfony</p>
				</div>
				<div class="tech-category fade-in delay-1">
					<h4>Type Safety</h4>
					<p>Zod, Effect TS, tRPC</p>
				</div>
				<div class="tech-category fade-in delay-2">
					<h4>Build</h4>
					<p>Vite, Turborepo, OXC Toolchain</p>
				</div>
				<div class="tech-category fade-in delay-3">
					<h4>Testing</h4>
					<p>Vitest, Playwright</p>
				</div>
				<div class="tech-category fade-in delay-1">
					<h4>Infrastructure</h4>
					<p>Docker, NixOS/Nix Darwin</p>
				</div>
				<div class="tech-category fade-in delay-2">
					<h4>AI Tools</h4>
					<p>OpenAI Codex, Cursor, Claude</p>
				</div>
				<div class="tech-category fade-in delay-3">
					<h4>Other</h4>
					<p>Astro, Jujutsu VCS, Git</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<div class="magazine-container"><hr class="editorial-hr" /></div>

		<!-- ========================================== -->
		<!-- HOW I BUILD -->
		<!-- ========================================== -->
		<section class="magazine-container" style="padding-top: 72px; padding-bottom: 72px;">
			<div class="fade-in" style="display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 20px; margin-bottom: 24px;">
				<span class="section-number">03</span>
				<div>
					<h2 style="font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 42px; font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.1; letter-spacing: -0.02em;">How I Build</h2>
				</div>
			</div>

			<!-- Principle 1: End-to-End Type Safety -->
			<div class="principle-block fade-in">
				<div>
					<span class="principle-label">Type Safety</span>
					<p class="principle-statement">If it compiles, it should work.</p>
				</div>
				<div class="principle-detail">
					Zod validates at the boundary. tRPC carries types across the network. Drizzle types the database layer. The result is a stack where a renamed field gets caught by the compiler, not by a user hitting a broken page. I aim for codebases where "undefined is not a function" is structurally impossible.
				</div>
			</div>

			<!-- Principle 2: Effect TS -->
			<div class="principle-block reverse fade-in">
				<div>
					<span class="principle-label">Effect TS</span>
					<p class="principle-statement">Errors belong in the type signature, not in the stack trace.</p>
				</div>
				<div class="principle-detail">
					TypeScript's try/catch is invisible to the type system — you can forget to handle an error and the compiler won't tell you. Effect makes errors typed, composable, and trackable through the entire call chain. It's the difference between hoping nothing goes wrong and knowing exactly what can. I use it wherever business logic has meaningful failure paths.
					<a href="/how-i-build/effect-ts" class="read-more">Read more <span>→</span></a>
				</div>
			</div>

			<!-- Principle 3: AI-Native Development -->
			<div class="principle-block fade-in">
				<div>
					<span class="principle-label">AI-Native Development</span>
					<p class="principle-statement">AI doesn't replace thinking — it replaces typing.</p>
				</div>
				<div class="principle-detail">
					OpenAI Codex handles most of my implementation work — I specify the task, it reads the codebase, writes the code, runs tests, and iterates. Cursor's Tab completion takes over when I'm writing code by hand. Claude helps me think through design. The skill isn't prompting — it's specifying tasks precisely enough that the output is mergeable.
					<a href="/how-i-build/ai-native" class="read-more">Read more <span>→</span></a>
				</div>
			</div>

			<!-- Principle 4: Local-First -->
			<div class="principle-block reverse fade-in">
				<div>
					<span class="principle-label">Local-First</span>
					<p class="principle-statement">Local-first is respect for the user.</p>
				</div>
				<div class="principle-detail">
					The app should work before the server does. In Studienbuch, students check their grades in classrooms where school Wi-Fi barely works. Local-first with offline sync and optimistic UI means the app never stalls on a loading spinner for data you already have. It changes the entire relationship between user and software — the data is theirs, and it's always available.
				</div>
			</div>

			<!-- Principle 5: Developer Experience & Tooling -->
			<div class="principle-block fade-in">
				<div>
					<span class="principle-label">Developer Experience</span>
					<p class="principle-statement">When the tooling disappears, you spend your energy on the product.</p>
				</div>
				<div class="principle-detail">
					Nix gives every developer the exact same environment — no "works on my machine," no broken installs after an OS update. Turborepo keeps the monorepo fast. OXC lints in milliseconds instead of seconds. I care about DX because every minute spent fighting the build system is a minute not spent shipping. Good tooling compounds over every commit.
				</div>
			</div>

			<!-- Principle 6: Jujutsu -->
			<div class="principle-block reverse fade-in">
				<div>
					<span class="principle-label">Version Control</span>
					<p class="principle-statement">Better tools make better habits.</p>
				</div>
				<div class="principle-detail">
					Jujutsu (jj) is a Git-compatible version control system that makes rebasing, splitting commits, and working on multiple changes at once feel natural. The built-in undo system means you can experiment freely. It removes the fear that keeps developers from writing clean, atomic commits — and once you've used it, going back to raw git feels like writing code without types.
				</div>
			</div>

			<!-- Principle 7: Shipping Quality Fast -->
			<div class="principle-block fade-in">
				<div>
					<span class="principle-label">Shipping</span>
					<p class="principle-statement">Speed and quality stop being trade-offs when the type system does its job.</p>
				</div>
				<div class="principle-detail">
